Fields use explicit types. `init` is the constructor and must return `{}`. Inside methods, fields are in scope without `obj.`, and `self` refers to the receiver.

Instantiate a class with `Name(args)`, then use `obj.field` for fields and `obj.method(...)` for methods.

```redb
class Point {
    int x
    int y

    init = do(int, int -> {}) {
        x = arg1
        y = arg2
    }
}

main() {
    p = Point(3, 4)
    writeln(p.x)        -- 3
    p.y = 10
    writeln(p.y)        -- 10
}
```

Fields are zero-initialized before `init` runs. Class objects are heap-allocated and are never freed.
